\begin{title}
3.2. Optical and photoelectrochemical characterizations
\end{title}

The optical and electronic properties of Por-Phen-COF and Por-Phen- COF-N+ were studied. Ultraviolet/visible diffusion reflectance spec­ troscopy (UV/vis DRS) showed that the Por-Phen-COF and Por-Phen- COF-N+ have a wide absorption spectrum (Fig. 3a), which attributed to the Soret bond and Q bond of TAPP (Fig. S9) [52]. Based on the Kubelka-Munk transformation reflectance spectra of UV–vis DRS (Fig. S10), the optical band gaps (Eg) of Por-Phen-COF and Por-Phen-COF-N+ are calculated to be 1.70 eV and 1.44 eV, respectively [53]. The decrease of Eg indicated that the cationization enhances the light-collecting capability. It is expected to promote the light utilization in photocatalysis. To evaluate the energy level of COFs, the energy band

