To in-depth understand the influence of COFs structure on the cat­ alytic mechanism, the dipole moments for most stable basic structure of Por-Phen-COF and Por-Phen-COF-N+ were analyzed by the DFT, which are 4.56 and 5.57 Debye, respectively (Fig. S36). The higher dipole moments of Por-Phen-COF-N+ indicate that local cationization affects the intermolecular polarity and contributes to electric field polarization [83]. This will promote the redistribution of charge within the COFs. Moreover, the frontier orbits of two COFs were analyzed. Results show that the HOMO of Por-Phen-COF is mainly localized on the TAPP unit (Fig. 6a), while the LUMO is localized on the PDDA unit (Fig. 6b), both

